      "writtenOn": "2023-03-23T13:06:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the plan to have an implementation of SkConvertPixels that does not use Raster pipeline? As of now, this means that to link code that uses SkBitmap and SkPixmap (at least), raster pipeline is also needed to be compiled and linked (as per my buffet build experiments).",
      "parentUuid": "6ec1b9f7_a6a02749",
      "revId": "96ba474a082cb73a511c9ac4d54c57e27579c04e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aba42a32_5f911ed1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-23T13:20:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the moment, no, but it\u0027s at least possible. The first version that Mike started writing had a bunch of dedicated conversion code, and I suggested changing it to use RP. That was motivated by two things:\n\n1) It really reduces duplication, particularly because the handling of many of our color-types is tricky, and having that code in multiple places is just more potential for bugs.\n\n2) We\u0027re already using RP throughout the code, including in the GPU backend (which has a corresponding GrConvertPixels, implemented similarly).\n\nRegardless, having this code use SkConvertPixels (rather than RP directly) feels right - if we ever want to fully sever the connection, we can add exactly one more copy of \"how to encode/decode each color type\" to that function.\n\nMore likely, I anticipate finding a way to isolate just the parts of RP needed for pixel conversions, while removing all the pieces that are only needed for actual CPU rendering.",
      "parentUuid": "09b4d204_2f522bbe",
      "revId": "96ba474a082cb73a511c9ac4d54c57e27579c04e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
